IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa4-general-duties.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 10, Chapter 2: General duties of directors (ss 170 to 181),
-- lines 2306-2411 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
--
-- SOURCE and HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa4-requirements.l4. Every branch carries its FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment.
-- The open-textured judgments in the general duties ("considers, in good faith", "reasonably diligent", "cannot reasonably be
-- regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest") are plain inputs: the text hands them to the director and the
-- court, and the encoding never guesses them. Each duty is a decision function ("the director has complied") and, where the
-- text states a duty with a "must" or "must not", also a regulative rule with no deadline (the text gives none) and no
-- consequence (the civil consequences are s 178, which points to the common law outside the sources).
-- Naming: every top-level name begins with the label of the provision it implements.

-- ---- s 170: scope and nature of general duties -------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The general duties, as the text lists them: "The general duties specified in sections 171 to 177".
DECLARE `s 170(1) general duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 171 the duty to act within powers`
    `s 172 the duty to promote the success of the company`
    `s 173 the duty to exercise independent judgment`
    `s 174 the duty to exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence`
    `s 175 the duty to avoid conflicts of interest`
    `s 176 the duty not to accept benefits from third parties`
    `s 177 the duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement`
    `s 170(1) a duty outside sections 171 to 177`

-- src:2308 | 170 Scope and nature of general duties
-- src:2309 | (1) The general duties specified in sections 171 to 177 are owed by a director of a company to the company.
@ref s 170(1) Scope and nature of general duties (src:2308-2309)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      duty IS A `s 170(1) general duty`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 170(1) the general duty is owed by the person to the company` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the company` AND NOT (duty EQUALS `s 170(1) a duty outside sections 171 to 177`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The general duties specified in sections 171 to 177 are owed by a director of a company to the company."

-- src:2310 | (2) A person who ceases to be a director continues to be subject—
-- src:2311 | (a) to the duty in section 175 (duty to avoid conflicts of interest) as regards the exploitation of any property, information or opportunity of which he became aware at a time when he was a director, and
-- src:2312 | (b) to the duty in section 176 (duty not to accept benefits from third parties) as regards things done or omitted by him before he ceased to be a director.
-- src:2313 | To that extent those duties apply to a former director as to a director, subject to any necessary adaptations.
@ref s 170(2) A person who ceases to be a director (src:2310-2313)
GIVEN `the person has ceased to be a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      duty IS A `s 170(1) general duty`
      `the matter is the exploitation of any property, information or opportunity of which he became aware at a time when he was a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is a thing done or omitted by him before he ceased to be a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 170(2) the former director continues to be subject to the duty` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person has ceased to be a director of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who ceases to be a director continues to be subject"
    ELSE CONSIDER duty
         WHEN `s 175 the duty to avoid conflicts of interest`
              THEN IF `the matter is the exploitation of any property, information or opportunity of which he became aware at a time when he was a director`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as regards the exploitation of any property, information or opportunity of which he became aware at a time when he was a director"
         WHEN `s 176 the duty not to accept benefits from third parties`
              THEN IF `the matter is a thing done or omitted by him before he ceased to be a director`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as regards things done or omitted by him before he ceased to be a director"
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names sections 175 and 176 after "A person who ceases to be a director continues to be subject" and does not say "only"

-- src:2314 | (3) The general duties are based on certain common law rules and equitable principles as they apply in relation to directors and have effect in place of those rules and principles as regards the duties owed to a company by a director.
@ref s 170(3) The general duties have effect in place of the common law rules (src:2314)
GIVEN `the duty is one owed to a company by a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 170(3) the general duties have effect in place of the common law rules and equitable principles` MEANS
    IF `the duty is one owed to a company by a director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as regards the duties owed to a company by a director"

-- src:2315 | (4) The general duties shall be interpreted and applied in the same way as common law rules or equitable principles, and regard shall be had to the corresponding common law rules and equitable principles in interpreting and applying the general duties.
@ref s 170(4) Interpretation and application (src:2315)
GIVEN `the general duties are being interpreted or applied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 170(4) regard shall be had to the corresponding common law rules and equitable principles` MEANS
    IF `the general duties are being interpreted or applied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in interpreting and applying the general duties"

-- src:2316 | (5) The general duties apply to a shadow director of a company where and to the extent that they are capable of so applying.
@ref s 170(5) Shadow directors (src:2316)
GIVEN `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the general duty is capable of applying to a shadow director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 170(5) the general duty applies to the shadow director` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 251 the person is a shadow director`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN IF `the general duty is capable of applying to a shadow director`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where and to the extent that they are capable of so applying"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The general duties apply to a shadow director of a company"; the person is not a shadow director
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a shadow director is s 251 (coa5)

-- ---- s 171: duty to act within powers -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2318 | 171 Duty to act within powers
-- src:2319 | A director of a company must—
-- src:2320 | (a) act in accordance with the company's constitution, and
-- src:2321 | (b) only exercise powers for the purposes for which they are conferred.
@ref s 171 Duty to act within powers (src:2318-2321)
GIVEN `the director acts in accordance with the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director only exercises powers for the purposes for which they are conferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171 the director has complied with the duty to act within powers` MEANS
    IF `the director acts in accordance with the company's constitution` AND `the director only exercises powers for the purposes for which they are conferred`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director of a company must— (a) act in accordance with the company's constitution, and (b) only exercise powers for the purposes for which they are conferred."

-- src:2318 | 171 Duty to act within powers
-- src:2319 | A director of a company must—
-- src:2320 | (a) act in accordance with the company's constitution, and
-- src:2321 | (b) only exercise powers for the purposes for which they are conferred.
@ref s 171 Duty to act within powers (regulative rule) (src:2318-2321)
`s 171 the director's duty to act within powers` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Director, Company, "act in accordance with the company's constitution and only exercise powers for the purposes for which they are conferred"
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 172: duty to promote the success of the company --------------------------------------------------------------

-- (2): where the company's purposes consist of or include purposes other than the benefit of its members, the reference in
-- (1) is to achieving those purposes.
DECLARE `s 172(2) object of the duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 172(1) the success of the company for the benefit of its members as a whole`
    `s 172(2) the achievement of the company's purposes other than the benefit of its members`

-- src:2330 | (2) Where or to the extent that the purposes of the company consist of or include purposes other than the benefit of its members, subsection (1) has effect as if the reference to promoting the success of the company for the benefit of its members were to achieving those purposes.
@ref s 172(2) Purposes other than the benefit of members (src:2330)
GIVEN `the purposes of the company consist of or include purposes other than the benefit of its members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 172(2) object of the duty`
`s 172(2) the object of the duty in section 172(1)` MEANS
    IF `the purposes of the company consist of or include purposes other than the benefit of its members`
    THEN `s 172(2) the achievement of the company's purposes other than the benefit of its members`
    ELSE `s 172(1) the success of the company for the benefit of its members as a whole`

-- src:2322 | 172 Duty to promote the success of the company
-- src:2323 | (1) A director of a company must act in the way he considers, in good faith, would be most likely to promote the success of the company for the benefit of its members as a whole, and in doing so have regard (amongst other matters) to—
-- src:2324 | (a) the likely consequences of any decision in the long term,
-- src:2325 | (b) the interests of the company's employees,
-- src:2326 | (c) the need to foster the company's business relationships with suppliers, customers and others,
-- src:2327 | (d) the impact of the company's operations on the community and the environment,
-- src:2328 | (e) the desirability of the company maintaining a reputation for high standards of business conduct, and
-- src:2329 | (f) the need to act fairly as between members of the company.
@ref s 172(1) Duty to promote the success of the company (src:2322-2329)
GIVEN `the director acts in the way he considers, in good faith, would be most likely to promote the object of the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has regard to the likely consequences of any decision in the long term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has regard to the interests of the company's employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has regard to the need to foster the company's business relationships with suppliers, customers and others` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has regard to the impact of the company's operations on the community and the environment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has regard to the desirability of the company maintaining a reputation for high standards of business conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has regard to the need to act fairly as between members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172(1) the director has complied with the duty to promote the success of the company` MEANS
    IF       `the director acts in the way he considers, in good faith, would be most likely to promote the object of the duty`
         AND `the director has regard to the likely consequences of any decision in the long term`
         AND `the director has regard to the interests of the company's employees`
         AND `the director has regard to the need to foster the company's business relationships with suppliers, customers and others`
         AND `the director has regard to the impact of the company's operations on the community and the environment`
         AND `the director has regard to the desirability of the company maintaining a reputation for high standards of business conduct`
         AND `the director has regard to the need to act fairly as between members of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director of a company must act in the way he considers, in good faith, would be most likely to promote the success of the company for the benefit of its members as a whole, and in doing so have regard (amongst other matters) to"

-- src:2331 | (3) The duty imposed by this section has effect subject to any enactment or rule of law requiring directors, in certain circumstances, to consider or act in the interests of creditors of the company.
@ref s 172(3) The duty is subject to creditors' interests (src:2331)
GIVEN `an enactment or rule of law requires directors, in the circumstances, to consider or act in the interests of creditors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172(3) the duty has effect subject to the enactment or rule of law requiring directors to consider or act in the interests of creditors` MEANS
    IF `an enactment or rule of law requires directors, in the circumstances, to consider or act in the interests of creditors of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to any enactment or rule of law requiring directors, in certain circumstances, to consider or act in the interests of creditors of the company"

-- src:2322 | 172 Duty to promote the success of the company
-- src:2323 | (1) A director of a company must act in the way he considers, in good faith, would be most likely to promote the success of the company for the benefit of its members as a whole, and in doing so have regard (amongst other matters) to—
@ref s 172(1) Duty to promote the success of the company (regulative rule) (src:2322-2323)
`s 172(1) the director's duty to promote the success of the company` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Director, Company, "act in the way he considers, in good faith, would be most likely to promote the success of the company for the benefit of its members as a whole, having regard to the matters in paragraphs (a) to (f)"
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 173: duty to exercise independent judgment -----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2334 | (2) This duty is not infringed by his acting—
-- src:2335 | (a) in accordance with an agreement duly entered into by the company that restricts the future exercise of discretion by its directors, or
-- src:2336 | (b) in a way authorised by the company's constitution.
@ref s 173(2) The duty is not infringed by acting under an agreement or as the constitution authorises (src:2334-2336)
GIVEN `the director acts in accordance with an agreement duly entered into by the company that restricts the future exercise of discretion by its directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director acts in a way authorised by the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173(2) the duty to exercise independent judgment is not infringed by the director's acting` MEANS
    IF `the director acts in accordance with an agreement duly entered into by the company that restricts the future exercise of discretion by its directors` OR `the director acts in a way authorised by the company's constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This duty is not infringed by his acting"; other conduct is for subsection (1)

-- src:2332 | 173 Duty to exercise independent judgment
-- src:2333 | (1) A director of a company must exercise independent judgment.
@ref s 173(1) Duty to exercise independent judgment (src:2332-2333)
GIVEN `the director exercises independent judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director acts in accordance with an agreement duly entered into by the company that restricts the future exercise of discretion by its directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director acts in a way authorised by the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173(1) the director has complied with the duty to exercise independent judgment` MEANS
    IF `the director exercises independent judgment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 173(2) the duty to exercise independent judgment is not infringed by the director's acting` `the director acts in accordance with an agreement duly entered into by the company that restricts the future exercise of discretion by its directors` `the director acts in a way authorised by the company's constitution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director of a company must exercise independent judgment."

-- src:2332 | 173 Duty to exercise independent judgment
-- src:2333 | (1) A director of a company must exercise independent judgment.
@ref s 173(1) Duty to exercise independent judgment (regulative rule) (src:2332-2333)
`s 173(1) the director's duty to exercise independent judgment` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Director, Company, "exercise independent judgment"
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 174: duty to exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence ----------------------------------------------------

-- src:2337 | 174 Duty to exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence
-- src:2338 | (1) A director of a company must exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence.
-- src:2339 | (2) This means the care, skill and diligence that would be exercised by a reasonably diligent person with—
-- src:2340 | (a) the general knowledge, skill and experience that may reasonably be expected of a person carrying out the functions carried out by the director in relation to the company, and
-- src:2341 | (b) the general knowledge, skill and experience that the director has.
@ref s 174 Duty to exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence (src:2337-2341)
GIVEN `the director's care, skill and diligence is at least that of a reasonably diligent person with the general knowledge, skill and experience that may reasonably be expected of a person carrying out the functions carried out by the director in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director's care, skill and diligence is at least that of a reasonably diligent person with the general knowledge, skill and experience that the director has` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(1) the director has exercised reasonable care, skill and diligence` MEANS
    IF       `the director's care, skill and diligence is at least that of a reasonably diligent person with the general knowledge, skill and experience that may reasonably be expected of a person carrying out the functions carried out by the director in relation to the company`
         AND `the director's care, skill and diligence is at least that of a reasonably diligent person with the general knowledge, skill and experience that the director has`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This means the care, skill and diligence that would be exercised by a reasonably diligent person with"

-- src:2337 | 174 Duty to exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence
-- src:2338 | (1) A director of a company must exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence.
@ref s 174(1) Duty to exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence (regulative rule) (src:2337-2338)
`s 174(1) the director's duty to exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Director, Company, "exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence"
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 175: duty to avoid conflicts of interest ------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (7): "any reference in this section to a conflict of interest includes a conflict of interest and duty and a conflict of duties".
-- src:2355 | (7) Any reference in this section to a conflict of interest includes a conflict of interest and duty and a conflict of duties.
@ref s 175(7) Conflict of interest includes (src:2355)
GIVEN `the conflict is a conflict of interest and duty or a conflict of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(7) the conflict is a conflict of interest for the purposes of the section` MEANS
    IF `the conflict is a conflict of interest and duty or a conflict of duties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Any reference in this section to a conflict of interest includes a conflict of interest and duty and a conflict of duties."

-- (2): "This applies in particular to the exploitation of any property, information or opportunity (and it is immaterial
-- whether the company could take advantage of the property, information or opportunity)."
-- src:2344 | (2) This applies in particular to the exploitation of any property, information or opportunity (and it is immaterial whether the company could take advantage of the property, information or opportunity).
@ref s 175(2) Exploitation of property, information or opportunity (src:2344)
GIVEN `the situation is the exploitation of any property, information or opportunity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company could take advantage of the property, information or opportunity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(2) the situation is within the duty to avoid conflicts of interest as the exploitation of property, information or opportunity` MEANS
    IF `the situation is the exploitation of any property, information or opportunity`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "it is immaterial whether the company could take advantage": the second input does not change the answer
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "This applies in particular to the exploitation of any property, information or opportunity"; "in particular" does not close the list

-- (3): "This duty does not apply to a conflict of interest arising in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company."
-- src:2345 | (3) This duty does not apply to a conflict of interest arising in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company.
@ref s 175(3) Transactions and arrangements with the company (src:2345)
GIVEN `the conflict of interest arises in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(3) the duty to avoid conflicts of interest applies to the conflict` MEANS
    IF `the conflict of interest arises in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This duty does not apply to a conflict of interest arising in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only that the duty does not apply to a conflict arising in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company

-- (5): authorisation by the directors, for a company that is not a charity (for a charity see s 181(2)(b)).
-- src:2349 | (5) Authorisation may be given by the directors—
-- src:2350 | (a) where the company is a private company and nothing in the company's constitution invalidates such authorisation, by the matter being proposed to and authorised by the directors; or
-- src:2351 | (b) where the company is a public company and its constitution includes provision enabling the directors to authorise the matter, by the matter being proposed to and authorised by them in accordance with the constitution.
@ref s 175(5) Authorisation by the directors (src:2349-2351)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `nothing in the company's constitution invalidates such authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's constitution includes provision enabling the directors to authorise the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is proposed to and authorised by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is proposed to and authorised by them in accordance with the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(5) authorisation has been given by the directors` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    THEN IF `the company's constitution includes provision enabling the directors to authorise the matter` AND `the matter is proposed to and authorised by them in accordance with the constitution`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the company is a public company and its constitution includes provision enabling the directors to authorise the matter, by the matter being proposed to and authorised by them in accordance with the constitution"
    ELSE IF `nothing in the company's constitution invalidates such authorisation` AND `the matter is proposed to and authorised by the directors`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the company is a private company and nothing in the company's constitution invalidates such authorisation, by the matter being proposed to and authorised by the directors"

-- (6): "The authorisation is effective only if (a) any requirement as to the quorum ... is met without counting the director in
-- question or any other interested director, and (b) the matter was agreed to without their voting or would have been agreed to if
-- their votes had not been counted."
-- src:2352 | (6) The authorisation is effective only if—
-- src:2353 | (a) any requirement as to the quorum at the meeting at which the matter is considered is met without counting the director in question or any other interested director, and
-- src:2354 | (b) the matter was agreed to without their voting or would have been agreed to if their votes had not been counted.
@ref s 175(6) The authorisation is effective only if (src:2352-2354)
GIVEN `any requirement as to the quorum at the meeting at which the matter is considered is met without counting the director in question or any other interested director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter was agreed to without their voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter would have been agreed to if their votes had not been counted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(6) the authorisation is effective` MEANS
    IF       `any requirement as to the quorum at the meeting at which the matter is considered is met without counting the director in question or any other interested director`
         AND (`the matter was agreed to without their voting` OR `the matter would have been agreed to if their votes had not been counted`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The authorisation is effective only if"

-- (4): "This duty is not infringed (a) if the situation cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of
-- interest; or (b) if the matter has been authorised by the directors." The authorisation of (b) is effective under (5) and (6).
-- src:2346 | (4) This duty is not infringed—
-- src:2347 | (a) if the situation cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest; or
-- src:2348 | (b) if the matter has been authorised by the directors.
@ref s 175(4) The duty is not infringed (src:2346-2348)
GIVEN `the situation cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter has been authorised by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(4) the duty to avoid conflicts of interest is not infringed` MEANS
    IF `the situation cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest` OR `the matter has been authorised by the directors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names two cases in which the duty is not infringed and says nothing of any other; whether it is infringed then is subsection (1)

-- (1): "A director of a company must avoid a situation in which he has, or can have, a direct or indirect interest that
-- conflicts, or possibly may conflict, with the interests of the company." The function says whether the director has complied.
-- src:2342 | 175 Duty to avoid conflicts of interest
-- src:2343 | (1) A director of a company must avoid a situation in which he has, or can have, a direct or indirect interest that conflicts, or possibly may conflict, with the interests of the company.
@ref s 175(1) Duty to avoid conflicts of interest (src:2342-2343)
GIVEN `the director is in a situation in which he has, or can have, a direct or indirect interest that conflicts, or possibly may conflict, with the interests of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conflict of interest arises in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the situation cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter has been authorised by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(1) the director has complied with the duty to avoid conflicts of interest` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the director is in a situation in which he has, or can have, a direct or indirect interest that conflicts, or possibly may conflict, with the interests of the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 175(3) the duty to avoid conflicts of interest applies to the conflict` `the conflict of interest arises in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `s 175(4) the duty to avoid conflicts of interest is not infringed` `the situation cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest` `the matter has been authorised by the directors` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director of a company must avoid a situation in which he has, or can have, a direct or indirect interest that conflicts, or possibly may conflict, with the interests of the company."

-- src:2342 | 175 Duty to avoid conflicts of interest
-- src:2343 | (1) A director of a company must avoid a situation in which he has, or can have, a direct or indirect interest that conflicts, or possibly may conflict, with the interests of the company.
@ref s 175(1) Duty to avoid conflicts of interest (regulative rule) (src:2342-2343)
`s 175(1) the director's duty to avoid conflicts of interest` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Director, Company, "avoid a situation in which he has, or can have, a direct or indirect interest that conflicts, or possibly may conflict, with the interests of the company"
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 176: duty not to accept benefits from third parties ----------------------------------------------------------

-- (2): "A 'third party' means a person other than the company, an associated body corporate or a person acting on behalf of
-- the company or an associated body corporate."
-- src:2360 | (2) A “third party” means a person other than the company, an associated body corporate or a person acting on behalf of the company or an associated body corporate.
@ref s 176(2) Third party (src:2360)
GIVEN `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an associated body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is acting on behalf of the company or an associated body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(2) the person is a third party` MEANS
    IF `the person is the company` OR `the person is an associated body corporate` OR `the person is acting on behalf of the company or an associated body corporate`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “third party” means a person other than the company, an associated body corporate or a person acting on behalf of the company or an associated body corporate."
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3): benefits from a person by whom the director's services are provided to the company are not regarded as conferred by a third party.
-- src:2361 | (3) Benefits received by a director from a person by whom his services (as a director or otherwise) are provided to the company are not regarded as conferred by a third party.
@ref s 176(3) Benefits from a person who provides the director's services (src:2361)
GIVEN `the benefit is received from a person by whom the director's services (as a director or otherwise) are provided to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(3) the benefit is regarded as conferred by a third party` MEANS
    IF `the benefit is received from a person by whom the director's services (as a director or otherwise) are provided to the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Benefits received by a director from a person by whom his services (as a director or otherwise) are provided to the company are not regarded as conferred by a third party."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only what is not regarded as conferred by a third party

-- (4): "This duty is not infringed if the acceptance of the benefit cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest."
-- src:2362 | (4) This duty is not infringed if the acceptance of the benefit cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest.
@ref s 176(4) The duty is not infringed (src:2362)
GIVEN `the acceptance of the benefit cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(4) the duty not to accept benefits from third parties is not infringed` MEANS
    IF `the acceptance of the benefit cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names one case in which the duty is not infringed and says nothing of any other; whether it is infringed then is subsection (1)

-- (5): the same inclusion as s 175(7).
-- src:2363 | (5) Any reference in this section to a conflict of interest includes a conflict of interest and duty and a conflict of duties.
@ref s 176(5) Conflict of interest includes (src:2363)
GIVEN `the conflict is a conflict of interest and duty or a conflict of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(5) the conflict is a conflict of interest for the purposes of the section` MEANS
    IF `the conflict is a conflict of interest and duty or a conflict of duties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Any reference in this section to a conflict of interest includes a conflict of interest and duty and a conflict of duties."

-- (1): "A director of a company must not accept a benefit from a third party conferred by reason of (a) his being a director, or
-- (b) his doing (or not doing) anything as director." The function says whether the director has complied; the third party is
-- the answer of s 176(2) and (3) (a MAYBE BOOLEAN input).
-- src:2356 | 176 Duty not to accept benefits from third parties
-- src:2357 | (1) A director of a company must not accept a benefit from a third party conferred by reason of—
-- src:2358 | (a) his being a director, or
-- src:2359 | (b) his doing (or not doing) anything as director.
@ref s 176(1) Duty not to accept benefits from third parties (src:2356-2359)
GIVEN `the director accepts a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit is from a third party` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the benefit is conferred by reason of his being a director or his doing (or not doing) anything as director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acceptance of the benefit cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(1) the director has complied with the duty not to accept benefits from third parties` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the director accepts a benefit`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the benefit is from a third party`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must not accept a benefit from a third party"; the benefit is not from a third party
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a third party is for subsections (2) and (3) and the facts
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
              IF NOT (`the benefit is conferred by reason of his being a director or his doing (or not doing) anything as director`)
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "conferred by reason of— (a) his being a director, or (b) his doing (or not doing) anything as director"
              ELSE IF `s 176(4) the duty not to accept benefits from third parties is not infringed` `the acceptance of the benefit cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director of a company must not accept a benefit from a third party conferred by reason of"

-- src:2356 | 176 Duty not to accept benefits from third parties
-- src:2357 | (1) A director of a company must not accept a benefit from a third party conferred by reason of—
-- src:2358 | (a) his being a director, or
-- src:2359 | (b) his doing (or not doing) anything as director.
@ref s 176(1) Duty not to accept benefits from third parties (regulative rule) (src:2356-2359)
`s 176(1) the director's duty not to accept benefits from third parties` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    SHANT `Action of a party` OF Director, Company, "accept a benefit from a third party conferred by reason of his being a director or his doing (or not doing) anything as director"

-- ---- s 177: duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement ----------------------------------------------

-- (5): "This section does not require a declaration of an interest of which the director is not aware or where the director is not
-- aware of the transaction or arrangement in question. For this purpose a director is treated as being aware of matters of which
-- he ought reasonably to be aware."
-- src:2373 | (5) This section does not require a declaration of an interest of which the director is not aware or where the director is not aware of the transaction or arrangement in question.
-- src:2374 | For this purpose a director is treated as being aware of matters of which he ought reasonably to be aware.
@ref s 177(5) Awareness (src:2373-2374)
GIVEN `the director is aware of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director ought reasonably to be aware of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is aware of the transaction or arrangement in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director ought reasonably to be aware of the transaction or arrangement in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 177(5) the section requires a declaration so far as the director's awareness goes` MEANS
    IF       (`the director is aware of the interest` OR `the director ought reasonably to be aware of the interest`)
         AND (`the director is aware of the transaction or arrangement in question` OR `the director ought reasonably to be aware of the transaction or arrangement in question`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not require a declaration of an interest of which the director is not aware or where the director is not aware of the transaction or arrangement in question."

-- (6): "A director need not declare an interest (a) if it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of
-- interest; (b) if, or to the extent that, the other directors are already aware of it (and for this purpose the other directors are
-- treated as aware of anything of which they ought reasonably to be aware); or (c) if, or to the extent that, it concerns terms of
-- his service contract that have been or are to be considered (i) by a meeting of the directors, or (ii) by a committee of the
-- directors appointed for the purpose under the company's constitution." "To the extent" is taken whole or not at all: the
-- caller states the facts for the part of the interest in question (fork F36).
-- src:2375 | (6) A director need not declare an interest—
-- src:2376 | (a) if it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest;
-- src:2377 | (b) if, or to the extent that, the other directors are already aware of it (and for this purpose the other directors are treated as aware of anything of which they ought reasonably to be aware); or
-- src:2378 | (c) if, or to the extent that, it concerns terms of his service contract that have been or are to be considered—
-- src:2379 | (i) by a meeting of the directors, or
-- src:2380 | (ii) by a committee of the directors appointed for the purpose under the company's constitution.
@ref s 177(6) Interests that need not be declared (src:2375-2380)
GIVEN `the interest cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other directors are already aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other directors ought reasonably to be aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it concerns terms of the director's service contract that have been or are to be considered by a meeting of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it concerns terms of the director's service contract that have been or are to be considered by a committee of the directors appointed for the purpose under the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 177(6) the director need not declare the interest` MEANS
    IF       `the interest cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest`
         OR  `the other directors are already aware of it`
         OR  `the other directors ought reasonably to be aware of it`
         OR  `it concerns terms of the director's service contract that have been or are to be considered by a meeting of the directors`
         OR  `it concerns terms of the director's service contract that have been or are to be considered by a committee of the directors appointed for the purpose under the company's constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director need not declare an interest— (a) if it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest"

-- (1): "If a director of a company is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a proposed transaction or arrangement
-- with the company, he must declare the nature and extent of that interest to the other directors." With (5) and (6): the
-- director is obliged to declare unless one of them says otherwise.
-- src:2364 | 177 Duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement
-- src:2365 | (1) If a director of a company is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a proposed transaction or arrangement with the company, he must declare the nature and extent of that interest to the other directors.
@ref s 177(1) Duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement (src:2364-2365)
GIVEN `the director is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a proposed transaction or arrangement with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 177(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 177(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 177(1) the director is obliged to declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the director is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a proposed transaction or arrangement with the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a director of a company is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a proposed transaction or arrangement with the company"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the answer under section 177(5)`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not require a declaration of an interest of which the director is not aware"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the director is aware is not known
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
              CONSIDER `the answer under section 177(6)`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director need not declare an interest"
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an exception in subsection (6) applies is not known

-- (2): "The declaration may (but need not) be made (a) at a meeting of the directors, or (b) by notice to the directors in
-- accordance with (i) section 184 (notice in writing), or (ii) section 185 (general notice)."
-- src:2366 | (2) The declaration may (but need not) be made—
-- src:2367 | (a) at a meeting of the directors, or
-- src:2368 | (b) by notice to the directors in accordance with—
-- src:2369 | (i) section 184 (notice in writing), or
-- src:2370 | (ii) section 185 (general notice).
@ref s 177(2) How the declaration may be made (src:2366-2370)
GIVEN `the declaration is made at a meeting of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 184 the notice in writing is in accordance with section 184` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 185 the general notice is in accordance with section 185` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 177(2) the declaration is made in a way the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the declaration is made at a meeting of the directors` OR `s 184 the notice in writing is in accordance with section 184` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 185 the general notice is in accordance with section 185` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The declaration may (but need not) be made— (a) at a meeting of the directors, or (b) by notice to the directors in accordance with"; the subsection permits and does not say another way is not allowed

-- (3): "If a declaration of interest under this section proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete, a further declaration must be made."
-- src:2371 | (3) If a declaration of interest under this section proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete, a further declaration must be made.
@ref s 177(3) A further declaration (src:2371)
GIVEN `a declaration of interest under this section proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 177(3) a further declaration must be made` MEANS
    IF `a declaration of interest under this section proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a declaration of interest under this section proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete, a further declaration must be made."

-- (4): "Any declaration required by this section must be made before the company enters into the transaction or arrangement."
-- src:2364 | 177 Duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement
-- src:2365 | (1) If a director of a company is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a proposed transaction or arrangement with the company, he must declare the nature and extent of that interest to the other directors.
-- src:2372 | (4) Any declaration required by this section must be made before the company enters into the transaction or arrangement.
@ref s 177(1) and (4) The declaration made as the section requires (src:2364-2365 and src:2372)
GIVEN `the answer under section 177(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the director declared the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration was made before the company entered into the transaction or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 177(4) the director has made the declaration the section requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 177(1)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any declaration required by this section"; no declaration is required
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a declaration is required is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN IF `the director declared the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` AND `the declaration was made before the company entered into the transaction or arrangement`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any declaration required by this section must be made before the company enters into the transaction or arrangement."

-- src:2364 | 177 Duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement
-- src:2365 | (1) If a director of a company is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a proposed transaction or arrangement with the company, he must declare the nature and extent of that interest to the other directors.
-- src:2372 | (4) Any declaration required by this section must be made before the company enters into the transaction or arrangement.
@ref s 177(1) and (4) The director's duty to declare (regulative rule) (src:2364-2365 and src:2372)
`s 177(1) the director's duty to declare the interest to the other directors` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Director, Director, "declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors before the company enters into the transaction or arrangement"
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 178: civil consequences of breach of general duties ---------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2383 | (1) The consequences of breach (or threatened breach) of sections 171 to 177 are the same as would apply if the corresponding common law rule or equitable principle applied.
@ref s 178(1) Consequences of breach (src:2383)
GIVEN duty IS A `s 170(1) general duty`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 178(1) the consequences of breach are the same as would apply if the corresponding common law rule or equitable principle applied` MEANS
    CONSIDER duty
    WHEN `s 170(1) a duty outside sections 171 to 177` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The consequences of breach (or threatened breach) of sections 171 to 177"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- what those consequences are lies in the common law and equity, outside the sources

-- src:2384 | (2) The duties in those sections (with the exception of section 174 (duty to exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence)) are, accordingly, enforceable in the same way as any other fiduciary duty owed to a company by its directors.
@ref s 178(2) Enforceable as a fiduciary duty (src:2384)
GIVEN duty IS A `s 170(1) general duty`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 178(2) the duty is enforceable in the same way as any other fiduciary duty owed to a company by its directors` MEANS
    CONSIDER duty
    WHEN `s 174 the duty to exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(with the exception of section 174 (duty to exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence))"
    WHEN `s 170(1) a duty outside sections 171 to 177` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The duties in those sections"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 179: cases within more than one of the general duties --------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2385 | 179 Cases within more than one of the general duties
-- src:2386 | Except as otherwise provided, more than one of the general duties may apply in any given case.
@ref s 179 Cases within more than one of the general duties (src:2385-2386)
GIVEN `it is otherwise provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 179 more than one of the general duties may apply in the case` MEANS
    IF `it is otherwise provided`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except as otherwise provided"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 180: consent, approval or authorisation by members ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2387 | 180 Consent, approval or authorisation by members
-- src:2388 | (1) In a case where—
-- src:2389 | (a) section 175 (duty to avoid conflicts of interest) is complied with by authorisation by the directors, or
-- src:2390 | (b) section 177 (duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement) is complied with,
-- src:2391 | the transaction or arrangement is not liable to be set aside by virtue of any common law rule or equitable principle requiring the consent or approval of the members of the company.
-- src:2392 | This is without prejudice to any enactment, or provision of the company's constitution, requiring such consent or approval.
@ref s 180(1) Consent, approval or authorisation by members (src:2387-2392)
GIVEN `section 175 is complied with by authorisation by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 177 is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(1) the transaction or arrangement is not liable to be set aside by virtue of a common law rule or equitable principle requiring the consent or approval of the members` MEANS
    IF `section 175 is complied with by authorisation by the directors` OR `section 177 is complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a case where— (a) section 175 (duty to avoid conflicts of interest) is complied with by authorisation by the directors, or (b) section 177 (duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement) is complied with"

-- src:2392 | This is without prejudice to any enactment, or provision of the company's constitution, requiring such consent or approval.
@ref s 180(1) Without prejudice to an enactment or constitution requiring consent (src:2392)
GIVEN `an enactment or a provision of the company's constitution requires consent or approval of the members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(1) subsection (1) prejudices an enactment or provision of the company's constitution requiring consent or approval` MEANS
    IF `an enactment or a provision of the company's constitution requires consent or approval of the members`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is without prejudice to any enactment, or provision of the company's constitution, requiring such consent or approval."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of an enactment or provision requiring such consent or approval

-- (2): "The application of the general duties is not affected by the fact that the case also falls within Chapter 4 (transactions
-- requiring approval of members) or 4A, except that where either of those Chapters applies and (a) approval is given under the
-- Chapter concerned, or (b) the matter is one as to which it is provided that approval is not needed, it is not necessary also to
-- comply with section 175 or section 176." The function says whether the duty still applies.
-- src:2393 | (2) The application of the general duties is not affected by the fact that the case also falls within Chapter 4 (transactions requiring approval of members)or 4A, except that where either of those Chapters applies and—
-- src:2394 | (a) approval is given under the Chapter concerned, or
-- src:2395 | (b) the matter is one as to which it is provided that approval is not needed,
-- src:2396 | it is not necessary also to comply with section 175 (duty to avoid conflicts of interest) or section 176 (duty not to accept benefits from third parties).
@ref s 180(2) The general duties and Chapters 4 and 4A (src:2393-2396)
GIVEN duty IS A `s 170(1) general duty`
      `the case also falls within Chapter 4 or 4A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `approval is given under the Chapter concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is one as to which it is provided that approval is not needed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(2) the general duty applies although the case also falls within Chapter 4 or 4A` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the case also falls within Chapter 4 or 4A`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by the fact that the case also falls within Chapter 4 (transactions requiring approval of members)or 4A"
    ELSE IF (duty EQUALS `s 175 the duty to avoid conflicts of interest` OR duty EQUALS `s 176 the duty not to accept benefits from third parties`) AND (`approval is given under the Chapter concerned` OR `the matter is one as to which it is provided that approval is not needed`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary also to comply with section 175 (duty to avoid conflicts of interest) or section 176 (duty not to accept benefits from third parties)"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:2397 | (3) Compliance with the general duties does not remove the need for approval under any applicable provision of Chapter 4 (transactions requiring approval of members)or 4A.
@ref s 180(3) Compliance does not remove the need for approval (src:2397)
GIVEN `a provision of Chapter 4 or 4A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(3) compliance with the general duties removes the need for approval under Chapter 4 or 4A` MEANS
    IF `a provision of Chapter 4 or 4A applies`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Compliance with the general duties does not remove the need for approval under any applicable provision of Chapter 4 (transactions requiring approval of members)or 4A."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "under any applicable provision of Chapter 4"

-- src:2398 | (4) The general duties—
-- src:2399 | (a) have effect subject to any rule of law enabling the company to give authority, specifically or generally, for anything to be done (or omitted) by the directors, or any of them, that would otherwise be a breach of duty, and
@ref s 180(4)(a) Authority given by the company (src:2398-2399)
GIVEN `a rule of law enables the company to give authority, specifically or generally, for the thing to be done (or omitted) by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has given that authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(4)(a) the act or omission is not a breach of the general duties because the company gave authority` MEANS
    IF `a rule of law enables the company to give authority, specifically or generally, for the thing to be done (or omitted) by the directors` AND `the company has given that authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "have effect subject to any rule of law enabling the company to give authority, specifically or generally, for anything to be done (or omitted) by the directors, or any of them, that would otherwise be a breach of duty"

-- src:2398 | (4) The general duties—
-- src:2400 | (b) where the company's articles contain provisions for dealing with conflicts of interest, are not infringed by anything done (or omitted) by the directors, or any of them, in accordance with those provisions.
@ref s 180(4)(b) Provisions of the articles for dealing with conflicts of interest (src:2398 and src:2400)
GIVEN `the company's articles contain provisions for dealing with conflicts of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing was done (or omitted) in accordance with those provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(4)(b) the general duties are not infringed by the thing done in accordance with the articles` MEANS
    IF `the company's articles contain provisions for dealing with conflicts of interest` AND `the thing was done (or omitted) in accordance with those provisions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the company's articles contain provisions for dealing with conflicts of interest, are not infringed by anything done (or omitted) by the directors, or any of them, in accordance with those provisions"

-- src:2401 | (5) Otherwise, the general duties have effect (except as otherwise provided or the context otherwise requires) notwithstanding any enactment or rule of law.
@ref s 180(5) Effect notwithstanding any enactment or rule of law (src:2401)
GIVEN `it is otherwise provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(5) the general duties have effect notwithstanding any enactment or rule of law` MEANS
    IF `it is otherwise provided` OR `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(except as otherwise provided or the context otherwise requires)"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 181: modification of provisions in relation to charitable companies -------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2402 | 181 Modification of provisions in relation to charitable companies
-- src:2403 | (1) In their application to a company that is a charity, the provisions of this Chapter have effect subject to this section.
@ref s 181(1) The Chapter has effect subject to this section for a charity (src:2402-2403)
GIVEN `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(1) the provisions of Chapter 2 have effect subject to section 181` MEANS
    IF `the company is a charity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In their application to a company that is a charity, the provisions of this Chapter have effect subject to this section."

-- (2)(a): s 175(3) for a charity: the duty does not apply to a conflict arising in relation to a transaction or arrangement with
-- the company "if or to the extent that the company's articles allow that duty to be so disapplied, which they may do only in
-- relation to descriptions of transaction or arrangement specified in the company's articles".
-- src:2404 | (2) Section 175 (duty to avoid conflicts of interest) has effect as if—
-- src:2405 | (a) for subsection (3) (which disapplies the duty to avoid conflicts of interest in the case of a transaction or arrangement with the company) there were substituted—
-- src:2406 | (3) This duty does not apply to a conflict of interest arising in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company if or to the extent that the company's articles allow that duty to be so disapplied, which they may do only in relation to descriptions of transaction or arrangement specified in the company's articles.;
@ref s 181(2)(a) Substituted subsection (3) of section 175 (src:2404-2406)
GIVEN `the conflict of interest arises in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles allow that duty to be so disapplied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction or arrangement is of a description specified in the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(2)(a) the duty to avoid conflicts of interest applies to the conflict, for a charity` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the conflict of interest arises in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This duty does not apply to a conflict of interest arising in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company if or to the extent that the company's articles allow that duty to be so disapplied"
    ELSE IF `the company's articles allow that duty to be so disapplied` AND `the transaction or arrangement is of a description specified in the company's articles`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This duty does not apply to a conflict of interest arising in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company if or to the extent that the company's articles allow that duty to be so disapplied"
         ELSE JUST TRUE -- "which they may do only in relation to descriptions of transaction or arrangement specified in the company's articles": the articles do not disapply the duty

-- src:2404 | (2) Section 175 (duty to avoid conflicts of interest) has effect as if—
-- src:2407 | (b) for subsection (5) (which specifies how directors of a company may give authority under that section for a transaction or arrangement) there were substituted—
-- src:2408 | (5) Authorisation may be given by the directors where the company's constitution includes provision enabling them to authorise the matter, by the matter being proposed to and authorised by them in accordance with the constitution..
@ref s 181(2)(b) Substituted subsection (5) of section 175 (src:2404 and src:2407-2408)
GIVEN `the company's constitution includes provision enabling the directors to authorise the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is proposed to and authorised by them in accordance with the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(2)(b) authorisation has been given by the directors, for a charity` MEANS
    IF `the company's constitution includes provision enabling the directors to authorise the matter` AND `the matter is proposed to and authorised by them in accordance with the constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Authorisation may be given by the directors where the company's constitution includes provision enabling them to authorise the matter, by the matter being proposed to and authorised by them in accordance with the constitution."

-- src:2409 | (3) Section 180(2)(b) (which disapplies certain duties under this Chapter in relation to cases excepted from requirement to obtain approval by members under Chapter 4) applies only if or to the extent that the company's articles allow those duties to be so disapplied, which they may do only in relation to descriptions of transaction or arrangement specified in the company's articles.
@ref s 181(3) Section 180(2)(b) for a charity (src:2409)
GIVEN `the company's articles allow those duties to be so disapplied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction or arrangement is of a description specified in the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(3) section 180(2)(b) disapplies the duties, for a charity` MEANS
    IF `the company's articles allow those duties to be so disapplied` AND `the transaction or arrangement is of a description specified in the company's articles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "applies only if or to the extent that the company's articles allow those duties to be so disapplied, which they may do only in relation to descriptions of transaction or arrangement specified in the company's articles"

-- s 181(4) is shown blank in the text (a row of dots).

-- src:2411 | (5) This section does not extend to Scotland.
@ref s 181(5) Extent (src:2411)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(5) the section extends to the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN Scotland THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not extend to Scotland."
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only that the section does not extend to Scotland
